    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter July 4th with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to maximize our 5x5 Roto upside. Our top-tier play today is **Cole Carrigg** (71.23), who benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against Robbie Ray. The combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and Ray\u2019s vulnerability to elite hitters gives **Cole Carrigg** the slight edge over **Kyle Tucker** (71.11), who also rates as an elite start against Wandy Peralta. **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) rounds out our top-three plays; he is in a prime position to capitalize on a massive SP_xERA gap against Sean Sullivan (6.43), making him a core piece of our daily offensive strategy.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46) on the bench. While his raw power profile is undeniable, a tough draw against Logan Gilbert combined with negative park factors forced the optimizer to favor the higher-efficiency projections of **Josh Jung** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom carry more favorable platoon dynamics for today\u2019s slate. We are keeping a close eye on the weather, specifically the rain risks hovering over the matchups involving **Gunnar Henderson** (42%) and **Brayan Rocchio** (37%). If these games face delays or cancellations, we have sufficient bench depth to pivot, though we are currently comfortable with **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite base projection despite the threat of precipitation. **Andy Pages** (69.99) also remains a high-conviction start, as we are projecting he can exploit Wandy Peralta\u2019s slow delivery to potentially generate stolen base value\u2014a critical, scarce category for our team's daily pursuit.",
